# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# BrandLoop dashboard — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env.local`. Both files are gitignored; this one is committed as the
# record of what the dashboard needs.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── REQUIRED ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# URL of the Express API this dashboard reads from.
#
# The dashboard never calls this from the browser — every request goes
# server-to-server through a Server Component or Server Action, because the API
# has no CORS middleware and a browser call would be blocked before it left.
API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080

# ── OPTIONAL ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Where "Add BrandLoop to Discord" sends the user.
#
# `integration_type=1` is the User Install flow, which is the one that matters
# here: the bot is in no servers, so it reaches users by DM, and User Install is
# what lets `/connect` work from a DM. `scope=applications.commands` only — no
# `bot` scope, so no permissions are requested.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ because the link is rendered in a Client Component and must be
# correct on first paint. The client id is public — it appears in any Discord
# OAuth URL.
#
# If unset, the "Add to Discord" button renders with an empty href and does
# nothing. There is no sensible fallback: this value is specific to the Discord
# application being deployed.
NEXT_PUBLIC_DISCORD_INSTALL_URL=https://discord.com/oauth2/authorize?client_id=YOUR_APP_ID&integration_type=1&scope=applications.commands
